      "urpx:hasCoverageClaim": {
        "@id": "sce:cc-care-2025-11-15",
        "@type": "urpx:CoverageClaim",
        "urpx:completenessResult": {
          "@id": "urpx:partial"
        },
        "urpx:selfContained": true,
        "urpx:explainedBy": {
          "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
          "@id": "sce:cc-care-2025-11-15-evaluation",
          "urpx:evaluationKind": {
            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "Special Condition 8 of Schedule TOU-D states a 32.5 percent discount off the customer's electric bill. That discount is modeled here, as a urpx:Price carrying urpx:multiplier -0.325 over the discountable subtotal of whichever SCE residential base plan the customer takes service under. The price names all eight candidate subtotals, four schedules at two effective dates each, read disjunctively so that the one present in the consumer's graph applies. Those subtotals are defined by the base filings rather than by this one; each holds the per-kWh charges of its plan, from eleven on Schedule D to twenty-two on TOU-D-PRIME at this date, and each omits three things: the Public Utilities Commission Reimbursement Fee, which Special Condition 8 applies after the discount; the California Climate Credit, which Special Condition 12 applies after city and county utility users' taxes; and the Base Services Charge, which this filing instead adjusts through two per-meter-per-day credits. Those two credits are part of the four line-item adjustments the same Special Condition grants, all four carried alongside the percentage: the Wildfire Fund Non-Bypassable Charge of $0.00595 per kWh, the Fixed Recovery Charge of $0.00198 per kWh, the Base Services Charge Surcharge of $0.063 per meter per day, and a Base Services Charge Discount of $(0.153) per meter per day. One priced benefit of Special Condition 8 is still unrepresented, and it is the reason this claim is partial: the exemption from the CARE Surcharge of $0.212 per meter per day. No SCE residential rate sheet in this corpus itemizes that surcharge, so there is no base charge for the exemption to cancel, and a credit written here would subtract from something the consumer never added. Two further provisions of Special Condition 8 are out of scope rather than missing: the application and eligibility declaration, and the rebilling of periods in which the customer did not qualify, govern enrollment rather than the price of service.",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-09-21T00:00:00"
        }
      }
    }
  }
